+# Result
+
+A nonzero curved scalar relative-equilibrium orbit is nonlinearly stable in an explicit positive magnetic-stiffness interval under the unchanged candidate action. It fills all simplex layers and has diamond holonomy -1. Its species norm is N; rho=sqrt(8+2sqrt(10)); the sufficient interval is 0<=kappa<N*rho*(10-sqrt(10))/(120*(6+sqrt(2))), with a>0. This follows from an exact ground-state transform and positive energy quadratic form transverse to gauge and global phases. The orbit is the unique global minimizing orbit at kappa=0.
+
+The all-rank result is a stable global minimizing SET, with nonflatness forced by a trial comparison when kappa/(r*N)<(rho-2)/18. Individual-orbit stability at higher rank remains open. Uniform ||h_U||<=rho sharpens the earlier bound four. The old nonzero flat family's instability remains valid.
+
+40 exact constructor checks and two numerical campaigns passed. Independent review pending; development lane with no registry entry; no physical normalization or experimental data; physical promotion 0.
